  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.48–0.65) vastly outperform image-only (0.21), and the best RNA config is multiprofile + scvi_n200 + avgpool (config_005, acc=0.650). The critical open question is whether the weak image signal (resnet50, acc=0.208) can provide complementary information when fused with the strong RNA signal, or whether it will dilute performance. This experiment (config_031) pairs the best-performing RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with resnet50 image features using weighted fusion, which lets the model learn the relative modality importance. If it beats config_005, multimodal exploration is justified; if it does not, we can deprioritize the 36 remaining multimodal configs and focus budget on refining the RNA-only space (e.g., config_006 for transformer aggregation with scvi_n200). Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image modality adds value at all is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question before committing further experiments to the multimodal branch."
}

